GLA (Graph-Language Assistant) - Licensing
==========================================

Copyright (c) ATEC (Advancement Through Engineering & Creation). All rights
reserved except as expressly granted by the license of each version.

GLA is PROPRIETARY. It is NOT open source. Every version is owned by ATEC and
is licensed, not sold, under its own GLA license. None of these licenses is an
open-source license (not MIT, Apache, GPL, Creative Commons or similar).
Getting a copy free of charge does not make GLA open source.

GLA was previously published under the name "CodeMind". Anything labelled
"CodeMind 1.0", "CodeMind 2.0" or "CodeMind 3.0" is the same model as GLA 1.0,
GLA 2.0 or GLA 3.0 and is covered by the same license.

Each version has its OWN license. A version's license applies only to that
version and to works derived from it:

  GLA 1.0  ->  licenses/LICENSE-GLA-1.0.md
  GLA 2.0  ->  licenses/LICENSE-GLA-2.0.md
  GLA 3.0  ->  licenses/LICENSE-GLA-3.0.md

GLA 1.0 is NOT released. Its license is an ACCESS license:
  - The model is not downloadable and is not distributed in any form, and the
    public gla-api library cannot run it.
  - It can be used only through access granted by ATEC (for example an API
    key to its server), including commercially inside your own websites,
    applications and API services.
  - Copying, modifying, sharing, selling or reselling the model, or reselling
    or sharing access to it, is not allowed.
  - Any copy of GLA 1.0 not obtained from ATEC in writing is unlicensed.

GLA 2.0 and 3.0 can be downloaded. Their licenses are MODEL licenses:
  - Commercial use is allowed for running your own services on websites,
    in applications and through APIs.
  - Modifying the model is allowed.
  - Giving copies of the model or a modified version to others is allowed
    only free of charge and only under the same GLA license - never under an
    open-source or any other license.
  - Selling the model or any modified version, in any form, is not allowed.
  - Public services must meet the safety and responsibility duties (3.0 adds
    transparency and security duties).

Common to all three:
  - Credit to ATEC is always required:
        Built with GLA <version> by ATEC
        https://github.com/ATECTechnologies/Graph-Language-Assistant
  - The names "GLA", "Graph-Language Assistant", "ATEC", "Advancement Through
    Engineering & Creation" and the earlier name "CodeMind" belong to ATEC and
    may not be used as the name of your own product.

The gla-api library (https://pypi.org/project/gla-api/) is licensed only to
run GLA models; it may not be decompiled or reverse-engineered.

The documents in docs/ describe the models; they are not licenses, and the
GLA 1.0 document does not make GLA 1.0 available. If a summary anywhere
differs from a version's license file, the license file governs.
